  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Among the following, the aromatic compounds are :</p><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt\"><img src=\"assets\\qt0277_bc33270584dd.png\" style=\"width: 325px; height: 159px;\" /></p><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt\">Choose the correct answer from the following options :</p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>)</mo></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>)</mo></math> only",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>)</mo></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>)</mo></math> only",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>)</mo></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi><mo>)</mo></math>&nbsp;only",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>)</mo></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>)</mo></math> only",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Aromatic compounds are considered as the compound which contains a conjugated planar ring system with delocalized pi-electrons cloud located at alternate double bond and single bond. For a compound to be aromatic it should follow Huckel&rsquo;s rule which says that the compound should satisfy&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi></math>&nbsp;electrons.</p><p>For Aromaticity, full conjugation of&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi></math>&nbsp;electrons&nbsp;should be there in closed ring.</p><p>(A) Non-Aromatic</p><p>(B) Aromatic</p><p>(C) Aromatic</p><p>(D) Anti-Aromatic</p>"
  }
}